! Cookbook — Recipe Manager & Post-Cook Journal

''Cookbook'' (`$:/plugins/mblackman/cookbook`) provides a native TiddlyWiki 5.4+ recipe workspace with live batch scaling, interactive *mise en place* checklists, countertop Cook Mode, and linked post-cook iteration logs.

---

!! Key Features

* ''View & Edit Template Body Cascades (`Recipe` & `CookLog`)'': Automatically renders any tiddler tagged `Recipe` in a two-column cooking workspace, any `CookLog` as a structured session report, and provides a guided 6-section Recipe Editor (status/rating pills, timing & yield steppers, equipment chip picker, visual ingredient row builder with bulk pipe-syntax toggle, and direction step/link helpers) plus a guided CookLog Editor when editing.
* ''Live Batch Scaling (`½×` to `3×`)'': Scales `base-servings` and pipe-delimited or inline `<<ing>>` ingredient quantities on the fly (including decimals and fractions like `1/2` or `1 1/2`).
* ''Ephemeral Mise en Place Checklists'': Check off prepped ingredients in `$:/temp/recipe/mise/...` without dirtying the recipe's modification timestamp.
* ''Countertop Cook Mode'': Enlarges typography and promotes all interactive controls to `44px` touch targets (`data-suite-density="touch"`).
* ''Pinned Kitchen Tweaks & Iteration History'': Record post-cook logs inline and promote `"Next Time"` lessons directly to the recipe's top callout banner with one click.

---

!! Ingredient Syntax

Populate the `ingredients` field using `qty | unit | item | optional note` per line, with `# Section Name` for sub-headings:

```text
# Dough (70% Hydration)
400 | g | [[Bread Flour]] | King Arthur preferred
280 | g | [[Warm Water]] | 95°F / 35°C
1/2 | tsp | [[Instant Yeast]] |
```

Or invoke the global `<<ing>>` procedure anywhere in WikiText:

```tid
<<ing qty="200" unit="g" item="[[Bread Flour]]" note="sifted">>
```
